title: The government has lost its majority!
subtitle:
new-page: true
on-arrival: 
tags: event
view-if: year = 1972 and month == 4
max-visits: 1

= The government has lost its majority!

Our <span style="color: #C00000;">Social</span>-<span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberal</span> coalition has lost the majority in the Bundestag! Many of our MPs don't agree with the Neue Ostpolitik and have joined the <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span>/<span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> faction.

- @vonc: The <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span> has called a constructive vote of no confidence...

@vonc

The <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span> has called a constructive vote of no confidence. If this succeeds, our chancellor will be replaced and we are forced to leave government.

- @vonc_outcome: Let us hope for the best...

@vonc_outcome
go-to: vonc_succeed if eastern_relation < 2; vonc_fail if eastern_relation >= 2

@vonc_succeed
on-arrival: chancellor = "Barzel"; chancellor_party = "CDU"; spd_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_social_liberal_coalition = 0; spd_toleration = 0; foreign_minister_party = "FDP"; foreign_minister = "Genscher"; interior_minister_party = "CDU"; interior_minister = "Benda"; justice_minister_party = "CSU"; justice_minister = "Jaeger"; labor_minister_party = "CDU"; labor_minister = "Katzer"; defense_minister_party = "CDU"; defense_minister = "von Hassel"; economic_minister_party = "CDU"; economic_minister = "Schmücker"; finance_minister_party = "CSU"; finance_minister = "Strauß"; agriculture_minister_party = "CSU"; agriculture_minister = "Höcherl"; coalition_dissent = 0; pro_republic -= 5; self_employed_spd -= 3; white_collar_workers_spd -= 2; workers_spd -= 2 if pro_republic < 50; workers_spd -= 2 if pro_republic < 40; self_employed_npd += 4 if pro_republic < 50; white_collar_workers_npd += 3 if pro_republic < 50

Willy Brandt is no longer chancellor. We have failed. For now...

@vonc_fail

Surprisingly, we have won the vote of no confidence! This bolsters our support. 

But who voted for us? Did some former MPs of our coalition change their mind? Or did someone else help us?
